@startuml 05_submit_review_ai_training
title Submit Post-Session Review → Trust Score + AI Weight Training

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #F9A825
}

actor "Reviewer (User A)" as User
participant "SubmitReviewFragment" as Fragment
participant "ReviewViewModel\n.submitReview()" as VM
participant "ReviewRepositoryImpl" as FERepo
participant "ReviewController\nPOST /sessions/{id}/review" as Controller
participant "ReviewCommandService\n.submitReview()" as ReviewSvc
participant "WalkSessionRepository" as SessionRepo
participant "WalkReviewRepository" as ReviewRepo
participant "ReviewTagRepository" as TagRepo
participant "UserRepository\n(trust score)" as UserRepo
participant "BadgeEvaluationService" as BadgeSvc
participant "AiTrainingService\n@Async" as AiSvc
participant "MatchingPreferenceRepository" as PrefRepo

== User submits review ==

User -> Fragment : Tap stars (1–5), select tags, optional comment, tap Submit
Fragment -> VM : submitReview(sessionId, ratingStars, comment, tagIds)
VM -> FERepo : submitReview(sessionId, ratingStars, comment, tagIds, callback)
FERepo -> Controller : POST /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}/review\n{ratingStars, comment, tagIds[]}

Controller -> ReviewSvc : submitReview(sessionId, reviewerId,\n  ratingStars, comment, tagIds)

== Validation (same transaction) ==

ReviewSvc -> SessionRepo : findById(sessionId)
SessionRepo --> ReviewSvc : WalkSession{status=COMPLETED}
ReviewSvc -> ReviewSvc : verify status = COMPLETED
ReviewSvc -> ReviewSvc : verify reviewer is participant
ReviewSvc -> ReviewRepo : existsBySessionAndReviewer(sessionId, reviewerId)
ReviewRepo --> ReviewSvc : false (no duplicate)

== Persist review + Update reviewee trust score (same transaction) ==

ReviewSvc -> ReviewRepo : WalkReview.create(...) → save
ReviewRepo --> ReviewSvc : persistedReview

ReviewSvc -> ReviewSvc : ratingDelta = \n  5★→+10 | 4★→+5 | 3★→0 | 2★→-10 | 1★→-20
ReviewSvc -> UserRepo : findById(revieweeId) → reviewee
UserRepo --> ReviewSvc : reviewee{trustScore}
ReviewSvc -> ReviewSvc : newScore = TrustScorePolicy.apply(trustScore, delta)
ReviewSvc -> UserRepo : save(reviewee{trustScore=newScore})
ReviewSvc -> BadgeSvc : evaluateAndAward(reviewee)

ReviewSvc -> TagRepo : saveTagMappings(reviewId, tagIds)

== Async AI Weight Training (fires AFTER transaction commits) ==

ReviewSvc -> AiSvc : trainWeightsFromReview(reviewerId, selectedTags)\n[@Async — separate thread]

note over AiSvc
    ⚠️ CURRENT BUG (Task 2.1):
    Loops over ALL tags. Each tag adds +0.05.
    Selecting 10 INTEREST tags → +0.50 to weightInterest.

    ✅ PROPOSED FIX:
    Use boolean gate — 1 signal per category per review:
    hasInterest? → +0.05 once
    hasBehavior? → +0.05 once
end note

AiSvc -> PrefRepo : findByUserId(reviewerId)
PrefRepo --> AiSvc : MatchingPreference or defaultFor(reviewerId)

AiSvc -> AiSvc : [CURRENT] for each tag:\n  INTEREST type → weightInterest += 0.05\n  BEHAVIOR type → weightBehavior += 0.05

note right of AiSvc #FFE0E0
    BUG: 5 INTEREST tags = +0.25 to weightInterest
    FIX: 5 INTEREST tags = +0.05 to weightInterest (same as 1)
end note

AiSvc -> AiSvc : normalize():
note right of AiSvc
    Pass 1: divide each weight by total sum → sum=1.0
    Pass 2: clamp any weight exceeding MAX_WEIGHT_CAP=0.70
    [MISSING]: Pass 3 — MIN_TIME_WEIGHT=0.25 floor (Task 1.4)

    Effect: weightTimeOverlap SILENTLY DECAYS
    because only interest and behavior are ever incremented.
    After many reviews, weightTimeOverlap → near 0.
end note

AiSvc -> PrefRepo : save(updatedPreference)
PrefRepo --> AiSvc : OK

== HTTP response returns before async training completes ==

ReviewSvc --> Controller : WalkReview
Controller --> FERepo : 200 OK {reviewId, ratingStars, ...}
FERepo --> VM : onSuccess(review)
VM -> VM : submitState = SUCCESS
VM --> User : Show success + dismiss review screen

note over User, PrefRepo
    Impact on Future Matching:
    • Reviewee's trust score is updated → affects S_trust score in next matching
    • Reviewer's weightInterest / weightBehavior updated → shifts W_* weights for next match
    • weightTimeOverlap decays silently (bug) → time overlap becomes less important over time

    Next time reviewer calls POST /intents/{id}/match:
    AiWeightedMatchingStrategy reads updated MatchingPreference
    → candidates are re-ranked with new W_* weights
end note

@enduml
